- Conservative / Transparent: “We currently hold $1.2M in cash and a reported net cash burn of $45K/month. This yields a headline runway of ~27 months. Finance reports a 30‑month runway after factoring in [briefly state adjustments — e.g., expected AR collections / removing one-time spend]. We recommend showing both the headline runway and a reconciled runway that documents those adjustments, plus downside and upside scenarios tied to collection risk and hiring plans.”
- Positive / Executive: “With $1.2M cash and a low net burn of $45K/month, Summit Software maintains strong runway (>2 years) while continuing to invest in growth. To be fully transparent, we’ll present the reconciled runway that captures timing of receivable collections and any non‑recurring items so stakeholders understand the assumptions behind the 30‑month figure.”

KPIs to show and track monthly
- Net cash burn (primary)
- Gross burn (payroll + opex)
- Cash collections (monthly)
- Days sales outstanding (DSO)
- Runway months (headline and reconciled)
- AR balance and expected timing
- One-time / non-recurring cash items

