- Burn trend drivers: Current burn reflects the net of (a) operating margin dynamics, (b) investment spending (R&D, product launches), (c) hiring and compensation, (d) one-time items (severance, legal, M&A costs), and (e) working capital / receivable timing. If any of these accelerate, burn will increase; conversely, efficiency gains, slower hiring, or improved collections decrease burn.
- Key message: With current cash and the stated burn, Summit has multi-year runway that allows for continued investment in growth, but we should not be complacent — verify receivables, contract prepayments, capital commitments, and expected seasonality. Plan to maintain a safety cushion and model scenarios for fundraising timing.

