Risks and mitigations
- Key risks:
  - Receivable delays or a major customer payment timing change
  - Unexpected one-time expenditures (litigation, vendor settlements)
  - Revenue concentration — a small number of customers making up a large share of revenue
- Mitigations:
  - Tighten collections and shorten DSO where possible
  - Delay or stage non-critical hires and discretionary spend
  - Negotiate extended payables with suppliers instead of across-the-board cuts
  - Maintain an internal reserve equal to N months of operating expenses (recommendation: 3–6 months of burn as buffer beyond stated runway)

